1
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:26,880
好，我们开始上课。大家今天一定要认真听，因为我今天要讲的所有内容都与期中考试非常非常相关，所以如果有谁今天没来上课，请把你们的笔记借给他们。
Okay, let's get started. You should really listen up today, because all the things I'm going to talk about are very, very, very relevant to the midterm, and so anybody who you know is not in class today, share your notes with them or something.

2
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:49,996
总之，我打算相当系统地梳理一下我认为很重要的内容，也就是自上次期中考以来我们学过的东西，而这正是周一期中考试的重点所在。那么，我们在上次期中考之后讲的第一个主题就是刚体运动。
Anyway, so I'm going to go through fairly systematically the material I think is important that we've done since the last midterm, and that's what the emphasis on the midterm on Monday is going to be on. So, um, this first sort of topic that we covered after the last midterm was motions.

3
00:00:49,996 --> 00:01:05,967
具体而言是 R^n 中的刚体运动，它们是 R^n 到自身的双射，并且保持任意两点间的距离。
So these are motions in R^n specifically, and they're these things that are bijections from R^n to R^n and which preserve lengths between any pair of points.

4
00:01:05,967 --> 00:01:12,120
也就是那种，比如只是旋转/扭动 R^n，而不会真正改变其中嵌入的任何几何图形的变换。
So these sorts of things that, you know, sort of twist R^n around without really changing anything that you may have embedded in it, for instance.

5
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:27,200
我们看到的是，如果你在 R^n 中有一个刚体运动——我们花了不少篇幅详细证明了这个结论是成立的，而且这是一个很重要的要点：任何刚体运动都可以写成某种标准形式，
And we saw was that if you have a motion in R^n—so we went through a certain amount of detail to actually show that this is true, and it's a sort of important point that any motion can be written in a sort of canonical form:

6
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:58,742
它可以表示为一个平移（可能平凡）、一个旋转（也可能平凡），以及某个固定的反射或恒等变换的复合。我们还指出了这些变换所属的群。
it can be written as the composition of a translation which is possibly trivial, a rotation again possibly trivial, and either some fixed reflection or the identity. And we sort of identified groups that these things belong to.

7
00:01:58,742 --> 00:02:10,800
例如，平移看起来就像是 R^n 中的一个元素，意思是，你只需选择要把原点平移到何处，这就决定了其他每一个点被平移到哪里。
So for instance, a translation looks like an element of R^n, I mean, you're just choosing where you want to translate the origin to, and that determines where every other point is translated to.

8
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:26,477
而我们所说的旋转，则是特殊正交群中的元素，它嵌入在正交群 O(n) 中，或者说是行列式映射在正交群 O(n) 中的核。
The things that we call rotations were these things in the special orthogonal group which was embedded or arose as the kernel of the determinant map in the orthogonal group O(n).

9
00:02:26,477 --> 00:02:48,080
所以大家务必要记住正交群的定义：等价地说，它是 GL_n 中满足其转置矩阵等于其逆矩阵的矩阵集合；换句话说，矩阵的列向量构成一组标准正交基。
So it's important that you remember what the definition of the orthogonal group is: it's, well equivalently, the set of matrices in GL_n such that the transpose of that matrix is its own inverse; or put another way, the column vectors of the matrix form an orthonormal basis.

10
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:59,519
我们还讲过双线性型理论，并看到了它是如何将“转置等于逆”的刻画与“标准正交基”联系起来的。
And we sort of had this theory of bilinear forms, and we saw how that connected the characterization by transpose equals inverse and orthonormal bases.

11
00:02:59,519 --> 00:03:18,560
现在，这个反射或恒等变换看起来就像是某个形如 {±1} 群中的元素，实际上 O(n) 就是积群……嗯，我的意思不一定是 ±I，而是某种正负号或反射，
Now this reflection or identity thing looks like an element of, well, a group like plus or minus 1; and in fact O(n) is the product of, well, I mean not necessarily plus or minus the identity, but you know, sort of plus or minus a reflection kind of,

12
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:37,680
或许我应该这么说：由某个反射生成的群同构于 {±1}，与 SO(n) 做半直积/直积这些部分结合在一起，就构成了所有刚体运动构成的群。
I should maybe put it this way: the group generated by reflection, this thing is isomorphic to plus or minus 1, direct product of these things, and then these things came together to form the group of all motions, so.

13
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:45,252
现在我们还看到了关于它的结构性性质。
Now we also saw something structural about this.

14
00:03:45,252 --> 00:04:06,440
例如，我们看到所有平移的集合（同构于 R^n——我的意思是很容易把它看作加法群 R^n 的一个副本）是所有刚体运动群的正规子群。
For instance, we saw that the set of translations, which is this thing isomorphic to R^n—I mean it's very easy to think of it as just being another copy of the additive group R^n—is normal subgroup of the group of all motions.

15
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:25,880
为什么？因为它作为从所有刚体运动群到 O(n) 的自然同态映射的核而出现。所以大家应该清楚存在这样一个映射。
Why? Well, it arises as the kernel of a natural map from the group of all motions to O(n). So you should be aware that there's such a map.

16
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:39,199
接着我们去研究了一种特殊情形：取 n = 2，研究平面中的刚体运动。
And we then went on to look at a sort of special case: we took n equals 2, and we looked at motions in the plane.

17
00:04:40,640 --> 00:05:10,090
这其中很大一部分内容是，首先分析平面刚体运动群的有限子群，进而深入分析平面刚体运动群的离散子群；最终我们对这些对象进行了分类，也就是离散子群的分类。离散子群。
So much of what that entailed was analyzing first the finite subgroups of the group of all motions in the plane, and then looking further at the discrete subgroups of the group of all motions in the plane; and ultimately we classified these things, so classification of discrete subgroups.

18
00:05:10,090 --> 00:05:25,640
请记住，“离散”意味着子群中任何旋转的角度以及任何平移的模长都存在一个正的下界（最小量值）。
So remember the discrete means that there is a sort of minimum magnitude to the angle of any rotation in the subgroup, and to the magnitude of a translation in the subgroup.

19
00:05:25,640 --> 00:06:00,600
这里的分析有一部分是将任意此类离散子群分解为一个平移子群（它是一个格点），以及 O(2) 的一个子群。
And part of the analysis here was via decomposing such a subgroup, any discrete subgroup, into a translation subgroup which was a lattice, and a subgroup of O(2).

20
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:04,720
我们刻画了究竟会出现哪些子群。
We characterized which ones actually come up.

21
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:22,040
顺便提醒一句：请大家务必去助教（CA）信箱取回批改好的作业，上周批改了大量作业，所以我想信箱都已经堆满了。嗯，让我看看。
So reminder: please do pick up your graded assignments from the CA mailboxes, there were a whole lot of assignments graded this past week, and so, um, the mailboxes are overflowing, I think. Um, let's see.

22
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:35,008
所以我想说的是，关于期中考试的复习准备：大家不必对此过分担心，也不必回头去死记硬背分类这些对象时的每一个细节。关键在于大家对整体脉络有个概念。
So I mean, just just a note in preparation for the midterm: you don't have to worry too much about this, and you don't have to go back and you know, memorize every single detail about how you classified these things. The point is simply that you have some idea of what's going on.

23
00:06:35,008 --> 00:06:54,999
我是说，光是把整个分类的证明从头到尾讲一遍，就要花上一个多小时，所以你们可以料到这不会是期中考试的考题，但大家应当了解这里发生的基本数学结构。
I mean it would take well over an hour to just, you know, go through proofs of, you know, the entire classification, so you can expect that that's not going to be a question on the midterm, but I mean you should be aware of the sort of basic structure of what's going on here.

24
00:06:54,999 --> 00:07:25,039
无论如何，出现的 O(2) 的子群——它们与可能的格点相互配合——是 C_n，以及我用的记号 D_{2n}，我相信在 Artin 的书里记作 D_n，其中 n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 6。
So at any rate, the subgroups of O(2) which arise—and these are somehow coordinated with the possible lattices—are C_n, and I'm using the notation D_{2n}, which is I believe the notation D_n for Artin, where n equals 1, 2, 3, 4, 6.

25
00:07:25,039 --> 00:07:36,119
事实上，我们得到了很多更深层的结构信息，我们将它们与其他可能的格点进行了匹配，但大家不需要对此过度担心。
I mean, in fact we got a lot more sort of structural information, we coordinated these things with other possible lattices, but you don't need to worry about that too much.

26
00:07:36,119 --> 00:07:56,360
好，接下来我们所做的是：我们在研究刚体运动时发现的许多性质，实际上都可以高度抽象化；而进行这种抽象对我们非常非常有帮助，因为我们可以找到各种各样有趣的集合供群在上面作用，比如群自身。
Okay, so then what we did is we said, well, a lot of the sorts of things that we discovered when studying motions can be really abstracted, and making this sort of abstraction will be very, very useful to us, because we can, you know, find all sorts of interesting sets for groups to operate on, for instance the group itself.

27
00:07:56,360 --> 00:08:08,560
因此，我们开始研究抽象对称性的概念，即群作用。
So we started looking at sort of notions of abstract symmetry, or group actions.

28
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:22,587
我们完全公理化了群在集合上作用的含义。
So we had a notion of what it means completely axiom—completely axiomatized what it means for a group to act on a set.

29
00:08:22,587 --> 00:08:27,960
这种弯曲箭头记号，表示的就是“作用于”，这只是一种方便的记号。
So this sort of curvy arrow thing, I just mean acts on, it's just a convenient notation.

30
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:35,008
这就是群作用，大家当然需要知道群作用的定义。
So this is an action, and you should know of course the definition of an action.

31
00:08:35,008 --> 00:08:59,248
它其实并没有提太多苛刻要求，主要是说我们有一个映射 G × S → S，并且单位元作用在 s 上（S 的任意元素）仅仅是将它映到自身；我们还要求复合满足某种结合律：
I mean, it in fact really doesn't say very much, it mostly just says that we have some sort of composition G cross S to S, and the identity element acts on s, just any element of S, just sending it to itself; and we demanded a sort of associativity for composition:

32
00:08:59,248 --> 00:09:16,313
如果我们用 g g' 作用在 s 上，应该等同于g 作用在“g' 作用于 s”的结果上；如果你只是随手写一个从 G × S 到 S 的映射，这绝非先验成立的性质。
so if we act on s by g g prime, that should be the same as g acting on g prime acting on s, which isn't, you know, sort of an a priori true thing if you just have a random function from G cross S to S.

33
00:09:16,313 --> 00:09:26,800
而这一点非常非常关键，它正是让你能够推导出所有关于群作用的结构性定理的核心。
And this was really, really very necessary, I mean it's what allows you to sort of get all the structural results about group actions.

34
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:48,839
因此，给定被作用集合中的某个元素，我们赋予了它几个非常重要的集合，其中之一是被作用集合的一个子集。
So given some element of the set being acted on, we associated a couple of very important sets to it, one of them being another subset of the set being acted on.

35
00:09:48,839 --> 00:10:12,480
给定这个 s ∈ S，我们有两样东西：轨道，它就是所有像构成的集合，即小 s 在群中各元素作用下的所有平移像。这就是轨道。
So given this s in S, we have a couple of things: an orbit, which is just the set of all images, all translates of this little s under elements of the group. So this is orbit.

36
00:10:13,639 --> 00:10:18,560
我们还关联了一个叫做稳定子群的概念。
We also associated something called stabilizer.

37
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:35,360
这就是稳定子群，它是所有满足 g(s) = s 的g ∈ G 构成的集合，而且它确实是一个子群。
So this is stabilizer, and this is the set of all g in G such that g of s equals s, and this thing is in fact a subgroup.

38
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:52,400
这两者之间联系非常紧密。我们所证明的，实际上是用这种语言刻画所有群作用的一种极其漂亮的方式。
And these things are very, very closely related. What we show is in fact there's a sort of neat way of characterizing all group actions in terms of this language.

39
00:10:52,400 --> 00:11:06,622
这里有一个命题：在陪集空间 G/G_s（即 G 模去某个元素 s 的稳定子群）上存在自然的 G-集合结构，要点在于：作为 G-集合，它同构于 s 的轨道。
So here's, here's the proposition: there's a natural G-set structure on the coset space G mod G_s, G mod the stabilizer of some element s.

40
00:11:06,622 --> 00:11:28,120
s 的轨道当然是一个自然的G-集合，它按假设满足群作用公理且是封闭的；一切都顺理成章，它在该作用下完全封闭，因为你就是这么定义它的。
And the point is that this thing is, as a G-set, isomorphic to the orbit of s. The orbit of s is certainly a natural G-set, I mean it by hypothesis satisfies the group action axioms and is closed; everything's fine, it's completely closed under this action because that's how you defined it.

41
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:39,378
那么具体来说这个映射是什么？它把陪集 g G_s 映到 s 在 g 作用下的像 g(s)。
So what's this map specifically? Well, it takes the coset g G_s and maps it to the image of s under g.

42
00:11:39,378 --> 00:11:48,880
所以这个映射是 G-集合（即带有 G-作用的集合）之间的同构。
So this thing is isomorphism of G-sets, in other words sets with G-actions.

43
00:11:48,880 --> 00:12:01,360
作为它的推论，例如我们看到它们的阶/基数以一种非常优美的方式相吻合，前提是满足有限性。
And as a corollary of this, we saw for instance that the orders sort of match up in a nice way, assuming you have finiteness.

44
00:12:08,639 --> 00:12:30,439
假定 G 和 S 有限——事实上只需假定 G 有限，因为那样轨道必然是有限的——我们得到基数大小关系：|G| 等于 |G_s| 乘以 |O(s)|，这也可以通过某种非常基础的计数论证得到。
So assuming finiteness of G and S—well in fact it suffices to assume finiteness of G, because then the orbit is necessarily finite— we have cardinality of size: the order of G is the order of G_s times the order of O(s), which you can also get by sort of a very basic counting argument.

45
00:12:30,439 --> 00:12:54,588
大家还学过另一个重点，那就是——这是一个非常有用的一类结论，可以在很多情形下加以应用——那就是如果你考虑一个元素的平移像的稳定子群，你可以通过共轭将其与原元素的稳定子群联系起来。
You also saw another important thing, and that is—this is a very useful sort of result, it's something that you can sort of apply in many cases—and that is that if you consider the stabilizer of a translate of an element, you can relate it to the stabilizer of the original element by conjugation.

46
00:12:54,588 --> 00:13:25,279
所以这是共轭子群，是由你平移该 G-集合元素所用的元素来进行共轭的；而且大家应该掌握一些基本的——我的意思是，虽然这并非极其重要，但复习这些公式的应用实例当然是非常重要的。
So this is the conjugate subgroup, conjugated by whatever you translated the element of the G-set by; and you know, you should know some basic— I mean, this isn't extremely important, but I mean it's surely important that you review some examples of applications of these formulas.

47
00:13:30,439 --> 00:13:42,280
而且绝对关键的是，至少大家要理解——不仅是理解，还要能够完全准确、清晰地写出我在这里写下的任何概念的严格定义。
And it's certainly absolutely critical that at the very least you have an idea—that you not only have an idea, but you'll be able to write down completely explicitly the definitions of anything I'm writing here.

48
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:51,680
如果你不清楚这里某个术语的定义，最好赶紧弄懂，因为考试中会有很多需要大家写出的定义。
If you don't know the definition of a word here, you better learn it, because there're going to be plenty of definitions that you have to give on the exam.

49
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:58,480
所以 G-集合就是赋予了群作用的集合。
So G-set is a set equipped with a group action.

50
00:13:58,480 --> 00:14:11,040
这个对象是一个 G-集合，因为它上面具有 G 的作用，所以“带有 G-作用的集合”与“G-集合”是同义词。
So this thing is a G-set because it has an action of G on it, so set equipped with G-action, G- set are synonyms.

51
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:48,800
嗯，好的。好的。现在让我们固定一个群G 和一个集合 S。这里我并没有先验假设 G 在集合 S 上已经有了某种作用，
Um, okay. Okay, yeah. So now let's fix a group G and a set S. So I'm not assuming that a priori I have some sort of action of G on this set S,

52
00:14:48,800 --> 00:15:02,111
但我想要对这些作用进行分类，也就是把集合 S 构造成 G-集合的所有可能方式；换句话说，G 在 S 上所有可能的作用方式。
but I want to sort of classify the actions, the possible ways that I can make this set S into a G-set; in other words, the possible ways I can have an action of G on S.

53
00:15:02,111 --> 00:15:38,199
定理是：G 在 S 上的所有作用与群 G 到 S 上的对称群的所有同态（当然是群同态）之间存在一一对应。请记住，S 上的对称群是 S 到自身的所有双射构成的集合，它构成一个群，我们很久以前就学过了。
So the theorem is: there is a one-to-one correspondence between actions of G on S and homomorphisms—these are supposedly group homomorphisms—from G to the symmetric group on S. So remember the symmetric group on S is the set of bijections from S to S, it forms a group, we saw that ages ago.

54
00:15:38,199 --> 00:15:42,040
所以这两类对象是一一对应的。
So these things are in correspondence.

55
00:15:42,040 --> 00:16:09,240
例如，如果给定一个特定的群作用——假设我们取 G 在 S 上的一个作用，那么它就对应于这样一个同态：它取 G 的一个元素，给出 S 上对称群的一个元素；而你要证明的是，映射 s到 g(s) 确实是大 S 到大 S 的双射。
So if we have for instance some fixed action—so suppose we take some action of G on S, then this thing gets mapped to the homomorphism which takes an element of G, and then we have to give some element of the symmetric group on S; and what you show is that the map s goes to g s is indeed a bijection from big S to big S.

56
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:14,040
然后我们必须验证这是一个群同态，但这并不难。
So we then have to verify this thing is a homomorphism, but that's not hard.

57
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:23,040
因此由该群作用诱导出了从 G 到 S 上对称群的一个同态。
So there's a homomorphism induced by this action from G to the symmetric group on S.

58
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:42,418
反过来，如果我们有这样一个——这样一个同态，它就被映射为一个群作用，其中 g 作用在 s 上定义为 φ(g) 作用于 s。
Going the other way, if we have such a— such a thing, um, this gets mapped to the action where g acting on s is defined by phi of g acting on s.

59
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:52,600
记住 φ(g)是从 G 到 S 上对称群的同态，因此我们可以把 φ(g) 作用在 S 的元素上，这就是我们定义群作用的方式。
Remember fee of g is a homomorphism from G to the symmetric group on S, so we can then apply fee of g to an element of S, and this is how we define the action.

60
00:16:52,600 --> 00:17:00,118
这是一套优美的双射对应，虽然看起来像是纯粹的“抽象胡扯”（abstract nonsense），但它实际上有非常有趣的应用。
This thing is a nice sort of bijective correspondence, and it just looks like some abstract nonsense, but it actually has some interesting applications.

61
00:17:00,118 --> 00:17:22,016
大家不妨至少思考一下如何应用关于 G 的阶与 S 的大小之间关系的观察，那会非常有用。
You might want to think about how one applies at the very least, um, observations about the relationship between the size of G and the size of S, that can be very useful.

62
00:17:22,016 --> 00:17:46,080
总之，这里有一个非常基本的注记：如果 S 的大小是 n，那么，我是说，S 上的对称群就是 S_n——虽然不是正则同构的，它依赖于把 S 的元素编号为 1 到 n，但这并不成问题。
So anyway, if there's just a sort of very basic remark: if the size of S is n, well, I mean, symmetric group on S is just S_n—not canonically identified, I mean it just relies on taking the elements of S and, you know, labeling them 1 through n or whatever, but that's not a big deal.

63
00:17:46,080 --> 00:18:01,280
所以要点在于，只要我们有 G 在 S 上的一个作用，我们就能得到一个从 G 到 S_n 的同态。
So the point is at least if we have some action of G on S, then we have a homomorphism from G to S_n.

64
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:25,077
这在 G 作用在自身上的情形尤其有用，比如通过左平移作用，因为它告诉你存在一个非常特殊的同态，一个足以刻画该群的、从 G 到 S_n 的同态。这是什么意思呢？
Now this is especially useful in cases where for instance G acts on itself by left translation, because it tells you that you have a very special homomorphism, one that characterizes the group, going from G to S_n. So what do I mean by that?

65
00:18:25,077 --> 00:18:43,919
具体来说，我们可以通过左平移让 G 作用在自身上。
Well, in particular we can act on G itself by left translation.

66
00:18:43,919 --> 00:19:03,600
如果我有一个 n 阶群，那么我就有一个群同态 G → S_n，并且我们还知道更多：它实际上是单射（Cayley 定理）。
So if I have a group of order n, then I also have group homomorphism G to S_n, and we know more about it: it's in fact injective.

67
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:17,659
这直接来自于：如果把这个映射记作 φ，记住在上述对应下 φ(g) 告诉你的正是这个作用的具体表现；
And that just follows because I call this thing fee: phi of G under this correspondence, remember, is just this thing that's telling you what the action is;

68
00:19:17,659 --> 00:19:35,000
但我们知道元素 g 实际上由它在群上的左平移完全决定；事实上仅由它作用在其中一个元素（单位元 e）上的结果就唯一确定了。
but we know that the element g is in fact determined by left translation on the group itself; in fact it's determined by acting just on one of those elements, the identity element.

69
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:39,840
所以这个同态是单射。
So this map is injective.

70
00:19:44,359 --> 00:20:12,720
现在来看 G 作用在自身上的另一个非常重要的作用：我想的是哪一个？共轭作用，太棒了！G 在自身上的另一个作用是通过共轭作用。
Now another very important action of G on itself: so which one am I thinking of? Conjugation, fabulous! Another action of G acting on itself, this one is by conjugation.

71
00:20:15,719 --> 00:20:29,640
换言之，g 作用在群元素 x 上就是共轭变换 g x g^{-1}。这是推导一个极其有用的公式的源泉，即所谓的类方程。
In other words, g applied to some element x of group is conjugate. And this is the source of a very useful formula, something called the class equation.

72
00:20:29,640 --> 00:21:05,600
所以如果考察 G 的阶，我知道可以把它分解为该作用下所有轨道的阶数之和——一般而言群作用都有这个结论，这里是对该作用下 G 中所有轨道求和——但是在共轭作用下，G 中的轨道被称作什么呢？共轭类。
So if I look at the order of G, and I know that I can break it up into the sum of the orders of the orbits for this action—I mean that's just sort of in general true, this is the sum over all the orbits in G for this action— but what do we call an orbit in G for the action by conjugation? A conjugacy class.

73
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:17,840
所以这就是类方程。
So this is the class equation.

74
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:23,840
大家当然必须掌握这个方程并能够加以应用。
You should certainly know this equation and be able to apply it.

75
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:59,840
特别地，大家应当清楚关于类方程的一个极其关键的事实：那就是大小为 1 的共轭类——如果我有一个大小为 1 的共轭类，那么我们就知道该共轭类中元素的特殊性质。我们知道什么？它属于群的中心 Z(G)。
In particular, you should be aware of a very, very critical fact about the class equation, and that is that conjugacy classes of order 1— if I have some conjugacy class of order 1, then we know something about the element of that conjugacy class. So what do we know? It's in the center.

76
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:24,840
这有几个非常漂亮的直接应用：例如应用于 p-群。大家应当知道什么是 p-群。
And this has some nice immediate applications: for instance to p-groups. You should know what a p-group is.

77
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:50,839
比如，我们由类方程可知，任何 p-群的中心的阶都大于 1（中心非平凡），而且我们还知道任何 p^2 阶群都是交换群。
So, for instance we know from the class equation that a p- group has center of order greater than 1, and we know other things like that every group of order p squared is abelian.

78
00:22:50,839 --> 00:22:55,840
这些都是非常有用的结论。
So those are useful sort of facts.

79
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:27,000
然后我们由此进入了另一个主题，它实际上与此密切相关：我们讨论了单群。换句话说，若 G 有一个正规子群，则该正规子群要么是平凡子群 {e}，要么是 G 自身。
Then we moved on to another sort of thing from this, which is actually fairly closely related: we talked about simple groups. In other words, G such that if I have a normal subgroup, that normal subgroup is either the trivial subgroup or all of G.

80
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:50,200
那么，要点在于这些群在结构上非常重要，原因有很多。
So, the point here is that these groups are structurally important for a number of reasons.

81
00:23:50,200 --> 00:24:12,640
但这里有一个它们在结构上很重要的例子：如果我有一个从 G 到 G'的群同态，并且假定 G 是单群，那么关于这个同态我们能断言什么？请讲。完全正确。
But here's an example of a reason why they might be structurally important: if I have a homomorphism from G to G prime, and I assume that G is simple, then what do I know about the homomorphism? Yes. Exactly.

82
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:29,880
完全正确。正如你所说，如果我们有一个从单群到另一个群的同态，那么我们知道该同态要么是单射，要么是平凡同态（将所有元素映到单位元）。
Exactly. So for instance, if we have, as you say, a homomorphism from a simple group to another group, then we know that that homomorphism is injective or trivial.

83
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:36,799
这正是我们在西罗理论中所借助的工具。
This is the sort of thing we leveraged in Sylow theory.

84
00:24:45,479 --> 00:25:15,840
关于正规子群和共轭类，我们还可以说得更多：如果 H 是 G 的正规子群，那么 H 实际上是若干共轭类的并集。
So there's something more that we can say about normal subgroups and conjugacy: so if H is a normal subgroup of G, then H is in fact a union—a union of conjugacy classes.

85
00:25:17,079 --> 00:25:27,079
这个结论非常有用，因为在某些我们可以明确写出类方程的情形下，它能帮助我们证明例如某个群不是单群。
And this sort of thing we found useful because it allowed us to show, in some cases where we could explicitly write out the class equation, that a group was not simple, for instance.

86
00:25:27,079 --> 00:26:18,960
例如，类方程再加上子群的阶必须整除群的阶这一事实——结合起来有时可以用来判定一个群是否为单群，我们见过这方面的例子。虽然这并不是特别重要，但大家最好能了解这个方法，万一需要证明某个特定群是否为单群。
So, so for instance, class equation plus the fact that subgroup of a group must have divisible orders—these facts together can sometimes be used to show a group is simple, we saw an example of this. This isn't really very important, but it's just—it's good that you be aware of this, should you ever need to show that a particular group is simple or not.

87
00:26:21,560 --> 00:26:37,920
好，继续往下看。接下来我们讲的是西罗理论（Sylow theory）。
Okay, let's move on now. Next thing we talked about was Sylow theory.

88
00:26:37,920 --> 00:27:08,309
记住西罗定理——这绝对是一类需要非常牢固背诵的内容，即便在睡梦中也能脱口背出西罗定理绝对大有裨益。也就是说：如果我有一个阶为p^e · m 的群，
So remember Sylow's theorem said—this is definitely a good sort of thing to to have very carefully memorized, being able to state in your sleep the Sylow theorems is definitely a useful thing: so if I have a group of order p to the e times m, where this factor,

89
00:27:08,309 --> 00:27:31,320
其中 p 的幂次因子非平凡，即指数 e ≥ 1，并且m 与 p 互素，换言之 p 不整除 m；在这些假设下，我们对西罗 p-子群就了如指掌。
this power of p is not trivial, so in other words the exponent is greater than or equal to 1, moreover this m is relatively prime to p, in other words p does not divide m; so under those hypotheses, then we know a lot about the Sylow p- subgroups.

90
00:27:31,320 --> 00:27:38,960
大家特别要掌握西罗 p-子群的定义，当然如果你连西罗 p-子群是什么都不知道，就不可能真正理解定理：
I mean particularly you should know the definition of Sylow p-subgroup, of course you can't really know the theorem unless you know what a Sylow p-subgroup is:

91
00:27:38,960 --> 00:28:13,160
西罗 p-子群（即 p^e 阶子群）的数目满足几条性质：首先，其数目模 p 同余于 1（n_p ≡ 1 mod p）；其次，其数目整除 m（n_p | m）。
so the number of Sylow p-subgroups, so subgroups of order p^e, satisfies a couple of things: first of all, number of them is congruent to 1 mod p; secondly, number of them divides m.

92
00:28:13,160 --> 00:28:21,919
我们见过很多极佳的例子，光是利用这一条性质就能获得大量有价值的信息。
We saw lots of great examples of how we could just use this fact, this fact alone gets you a lot of information.

93
00:28:23,479 --> 00:28:27,679
但能说的远不止这些。
But a lot more can be said.

94
00:28:27,679 --> 00:28:54,120
例如，任意两个西罗 p-子群都相互共轭，这也是一个非常实用的性质；还有一个在初等应用中不常使用、但在进阶应用中很有用的性质是：
For instance, every two Sylow p- subgroups are conjugate, is also a very useful sort of fact; and one that doesn't get taken advantage of quite so often in basic applications,

95
00:28:54,120 --> 00:29:41,213
若 G 中有一个子群 H其阶能被 p 整除，那么存在 G 的一个西罗 p-子群 P 使得它与该子群的交（P ∩ H）是该子群的一个西罗 p-子群，明白吗？
but can be useful in less basic applications, is that if I have a subgroup G— with order divisible by p, then there is a Sylow p-subgroup of G such that its intersection with this subgroup is a Sylow p-subgroup of it, okay?

96
00:29:42,920 --> 00:30:09,840
顺便提一句：回想一下比如这个结论——我们可以从第一部分推导出，例如西罗 p-子群的数目必为 1，进而推得在此情形下该西罗 p-子群是正规子群；这绝对是一个非常有用的必须记住的结论。
Just one remark: I mean recall that for instance this is the result—I mean we can draw from this first part things like that the number of Sylow p-subgroups must be 1, and then we can draw from this that in that case the Sylow p-subgroup is normal; so that's a definitely useful thing to remember.

97
00:30:14,359 --> 00:30:50,839
然后这是我们见过的几个应用：几个应用：我们看到的第一个应用是关于 pq 阶群，其中 p < q 为素数。大家绝对必须掌握这个。
And so here are a couple of applications we saw: a couple of applications: so the first application we saw was to groups of order pq where p < q are primes. You should definitely know this.

98
00:30:50,839 --> 00:30:58,799
例如我们知道西罗 q-子群的数目必为 1。
So we know for instance that the number of Sylow q-subgroups is 1.

99
00:31:01,079 --> 00:31:08,280
我们还简要讨论了 12 阶群。
We also took a brief look at groups of order 12.

100
00:31:08,280 --> 00:31:12,720
这对于期中考试来说内容似乎相当庞大了！
That seems like an awful lot to put on a midterm!

101
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:29,600
好，接下来我们学的是S_n 中的共轭。
Okay, next thing we saw was conjugacy in S_n.

102
00:31:30,839 --> 00:31:49,039
我们在 S_n 中反复使用的基础结构性定理是：任何置换都具有不相交轮换分解。
So the underlying—the underlying structural result about S_n that we sort of use repeatedly is that any permutation has a disjoint cycle decomposition.

103
00:31:55,733 --> 00:32:20,960
如果我有一个 n 个文字上的置换，我可以将其重写为乘积，比如 (a_{11} ... a_{1 \ell_1}) ... (a_{k1}... a_{k \ell_k})，其中这些是不相交的轮换。
If I have some permutation on n letters, I can rewrite it as a product, say (a_{11} ... a_{1 \ell_1}) ... (a_{k1} ... a_{k \ell_k}), where these are disjoint cycles.

104
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:43,586
当然，“不相交”意味着支集——即我在轮换记号中列出的元素集合——交集为空，所以它们是不相交的。
Of course disjoint means that the support, the things that I list in this notation for the cycle, have trivial intersection, have empty intersection, so they're disjoint.

105
00:32:43,586 --> 00:32:51,479
由此我们获得了关于共轭的大量信息：我们可以明确写出共轭的作用机制。
And then from this we get a lot of information about conjugacy: we can write down exactly what conjugation means.

106
00:32:51,479 --> 00:33:12,880
用 S_n 中的某个元素（置换）τ 进行共轭，对不相交轮换分解具有一种直观可见的作用：如果我进行共轭，
So conjugation by some element tau in S_n, some other permutation, has a sort of visible effect on the disjoint cycle decomposition:

107
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:41,519
该元素的不相交轮换分解就是 (τ(a_{11}) ... τ(a_{1 \ell_1})) ... (τ(a_{k1}) ...τ(a_{k \ell_k}))。大家应该很清楚我的意思。
so if I conjugate, this thing has disjoint cycle decomposition (tau(a_{11}) ... tau(a_{1 \ell_1})) ... (tau(a_{k1}) ... tau(a_{k \ell_k})). Well, it's pretty obvious what I'm saying.

108
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:53,840
然后我们进入了环论。
Then we moved on to ring theory.

109
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:09,883
关于环：环是具有两种相互交互运算的代数结构。
So rings: rings are things with two interacting operations.

110
00:34:09,883 --> 00:34:23,919
它们具有加法运算“+”，在加法下是一个交换群，并且具有记作 0 的加法单位元。
So they have this plus operation which is an abelian group, and we have an identity element which is denoted 0.

111
00:34:23,919 --> 00:34:49,159
然后还有乘法运算，它满足结合律并且自身具有单位元 1；但请注意，我们并不要求元素都有乘法逆元；事实上，对整个环 R 要求普遍存在乘法逆元是相当荒谬的，因为不难证明 0 绝不可能有逆元。
Then there's a multiplication operation which is associative and has an identity of its own, 1; but notice that we don't for instance request that there are inverses; in fact it would be quite silly to in general request inverses on all of R, because it's not hard to show that 0 couldn't possibly have an inverse.

112
00:34:49,159 --> 00:34:55,625
当然这两种运算必须相互关联，所以我们要求满足分配律。
And then of course these have to interact, so we demand some sort of distributivity property.

113
00:34:55,625 --> 00:35:25,079
此外为了获得良好的结构性结论，我们通常还假设乘法满足交换律——具体说是乘法运算的交换性，尽管我们通常会明确说明是否假定可交换。
And moreover we generally assume, in order to get good structural results, we generally assume commutativity as well— specifically commutativity of the multiplication operation, although I mean of course we'll sort of explicitly say if we're assuming that or not.

114
00:35:25,079 --> 00:35:37,617
那么——从环的定义中自然引申出了同态和理想的概念。
So what— well, we had notion of homomorphism and ideal that sort of came naturally out of the definition of ring.

115
00:35:37,617 --> 00:36:02,160
关于环同态，我就不重新给完整定义了，只需指出它们保持加法群结构、保持乘法，并且保持单位元 1；而把保持 1 列为独立的条件是必要的，因为在乘法下它并不是群。然后我们学了理想。
So there are homomorphisms, I won't define them for you, except to notate that they preserve the additive group structure, they preserve the multiplication, and they preserve 1; and it's necessary to make this as a separate hypothesis from this, because it's not a group under multiplication. And we saw ideals.

116
00:36:03,639 --> 00:36:07,240
理想是什么？
So what are these things?

117
00:36:07,240 --> 00:36:27,839
它们是加法群（即环在加法运算下）的子群，并且在环 R 的任意乘法作用下保持稳定（即吸收律 rI ⊆ I）。
Well, they're subgroups of the additive group, in other words of the ring under the addition operation, and they're stable under multiplication by R.

118
00:36:31,480 --> 00:36:46,219
它们是正规子群在环论中的类似物。然而在考试中，如果对理想的定义仅仅回答：它是环论中正规子群的类似物，那是远远不够的！
And these things were analogs of normal subgroups. However, on an exam it would not be sufficient for instance to say for the definition of an ideal: it's the analog for rings of a normal subgroup!

119
00:36:46,219 --> 00:36:48,680
你必须完整清晰地写出具体定义。
You want to actually explicitly give the definition.

120
00:36:48,680 --> 00:37:19,520
但关于它们有以下几条重要结论：任意环同态的核都是一个理想；并且该命题有逆命题，因为我们学过良定义的商环构造；该商环构造特别蕴含了：
But here are some useful facts about them: the kernel of any homomorphism is an ideal, but there's a converse to that statement, because we saw that there's a good quotient construction; and that quotient construction implies in particular

121
00:37:19,520 --> 00:37:50,600
每个理想 I 都是某个同态的核；实际上我们可以明确写出以 I 为核的同态，即自然投影映射 R → R-bar，即商环 R/I。
that every ideal I is kernel of some homomorphism; but in fact we can explicitly write down a homomorphism which has I as a kernel, namely the natural projection map R goes to R-bar, which is R mod I, the quotient.

122
00:37:50,600 --> 00:38:17,800
大家应当记住什么是主理想（principal ideal）：这是一种特定类型的理想，并非所有理想都必定是主理想，尽管有些环中每个理想都是主理想——稍后我们会重温这一点。
And you should remember what a principal ideal is: this is a specific type of ideal, not all ideals are necessarily principal, although there are rings in which every ideal is principal—repeat that in a minute.

123
00:38:17,800 --> 00:39:09,359
这里有一个重要的命题：如果我有一个交换环，那么该环是一个域当且仅当——什么？不好意思？当且仅当该环恰好有两个理想，恰好有两个理想，恰好有两个理想：即零理想 (0) 和单位理想 (1)（即整个环）。
So here's an important proposition: if I have a commutative ring, then that ring is a field if and only if—what, sorry? If and only if this ring has exactly two ideals, exactly two ideals, exactly two ideals: namely (0) and the unit ideal (1), which is all of the ring.

124
00:39:11,399 --> 00:39:24,160
刚才我提示了一个问题：即理想何时总为主理想？对哪些环而言理想总是主理想？
So I hinted at the question a second ago: namely when are ideals always principal? For what rings are ideals always principal?

125
00:39:25,720 --> 00:39:38,079
理想何时总为主理想？当时的主要工具是欧几里得辗转相除法。
When are ideals principal? And the main tool there was the Euclidean algorithm.

126
00:39:38,079 --> 00:40:00,400
欧几里得算法例如蕴含了：整数环 Z 的每一个理想都是主理想（Z 是 PID）。
So Euclidean algorithm implied for instance that every ideal of the ring of integers is principal.

127
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:16,288
另一个很好的情形：当 F 是一个域时，我们发现 F 上的多项式环存在欧几里得除法。
Another good case: when F is a field, we found that there was a Euclidean algorithm on the ring of polynomials over F.

128
00:40:16,288 --> 00:41:07,879
所以存在针对F[x]（即系数在 F 中的多项式环）的欧几里得带余除法，这蕴含了 F[x] 的每一个理想都是主理想，其证明与整数环完全类似，都是利用基本的欧几里得算法。
So there is a Euclidean algorithm for F[x], the ring of polynomials with coefficients in F, and that implies that every ideal of F[x] is principal, by the same sort of argument as for the ring of integers, sort of basic Euclidean algorithm thing.

129
00:41:07,879 --> 00:41:29,839
我们在课堂上深入讨论了商环，并且研究了商环的理想集合与原环的理想集合之间的重要关系：即商环的理想对应定理。
Now we've talked a good deal about quotients in class, and we also saw something important about the relationship between the set of ideals of a quotient ring and the ideals of the original ring: so ideals of quotients.

130
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:44,240
假设有一个理想 I。固定这个条件：固定交换环 R 的一个理想 I。
Suppose I have some ideal I. Fix this thing: fix I subset of R, ideal in a commutative ring.

131
00:41:44,240 --> 00:42:22,680
我们得到的结构性结论是：商环 R/I 的理想与 R 中包含 I 的理想 J 之间存在一一对应，并且这一对应是由从原环到其商环的自然同态来实现的。
The structural result we found was that the ideals of the quotient of R by I correspond to the ideals J of R containing I, and this correspondence is realized by the natural homomorphism from the ring to its quotient.

132
00:42:22,680 --> 00:42:40,434
如果用 f 表示典范投影映射，那么给定 R-bar 的一个理想 J-bar，它被映为其原像 f^{-1}(J-bar)。
So if f denotes the canonical map, then given some J-bar, an ideal of R-bar, this thing gets mapped to its inverse image.

133
00:42:40,434 --> 00:43:02,960
反过来，如果我有一个包含 I 的理想 J ⊆ R，那么只需考虑它的直接像 f(J)；并且第一同构定理告诉了我们更多：
Going the other way, if I have an ideal of R which contains I, then I just consider its direct image f(J); and the first isomorphism theorem tells us more:

134
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:18,023
它告诉我们这是一个非常优美的对应，因为 R/J 典范同构于 (R/I)/(J/I)（即 R-bar/J-bar）。
tells us that this is a really, really good correspondence, because R mod J is canonically isomorphic to R-bar mod J-bar.

135
00:43:18,023 --> 00:43:42,480
这就是由 R → R-bar = R/I 复合到 R-bar/J-bar 所诱导的映射，要点在于该映射是满射，其核恰好是 J，因此由第一同构定理，存在这样一个典范同构。
So this is the map induced by R going to R-bar equals R mod I, going to R-bar mod J-bar, point being this map is surjective with kernel J, and so by the first isomorphism theorem there's a canonical map like this.

136
00:43:44,280 --> 00:43:50,079
然后我们开始讨论“人为添加关系”（creating relations）。
Then we started talking about creating relations.

137
00:43:52,040 --> 00:43:59,480
我接下来要讲一个极其简单的例子，大家课后应当思考更复杂一些的例子。
So I'm going to talk about a much too simple example, so you should think about somewhat more complicated examples.

138
00:43:59,480 --> 00:44:09,839
这是添加关系的一个极简单的例子。
So here's a very simple example of creating relations.

139
00:44:16,760 --> 00:44:46,378
命题是：如果我有一个域 F，考虑系数在 F 中的多项式环 F[x]，并且我们添加关系让 x = 0，那么你觉得这个商环长什么样？它就同构于 F，完全正确。
So here's the proposition: that if I have some field F, I consider the ring of polynomials with coefficients in F, and I make the relation that x is equal to 0, then what do you think this ring looks like? It just looks like F again, exactly.

140
00:44:46,378 --> 00:44:55,200
直观上的解释是：我们添加了关系“令 x = 0”。
So the heuristic reason for this is that we've added the relation: make x equal to 0.

141
00:44:55,200 --> 00:45:08,600
记住作商运算的本质就是：当你模去某个对象作商时，你就是在说把该理想、正规子群或你用来作商的任何对象中的所有元素，全都令其为 0。
I mean remember that's what quotienting does: when you quotient by something, you're saying take all the things in the ideal, or the normal subgroup or whatever that you're quotienting by, and make them all 0.

142
00:45:08,600 --> 00:45:15,280
所以 x 被置为 0，但大家必须能够严格证明这一点。
So x is made equal to 0, but you should be able to prove this.

143
00:45:15,280 --> 00:45:28,560
在考试中仅凭直觉说“这等于令 x 为 0，所以自然成立”是不够充分的，因为正如大家在上次作业中所发现的，这其实是非常微妙的。
It's insufficient on an exam to say, well heuristically this is making x equal to 0, therefore it all works out, because as you discovered on the last homework assignment, this is actually a very subtle sort of thing.

144
00:45:28,560 --> 00:45:39,720
如果我取 F[x] 模去比如 x^2 - 1，我得到的并不是 F，尽管表面上看我似乎只是添加了关系 x = 1。
If I take F[x] and I mod out by x^2 - 1 for instance, I don't get F, even though it looks like I'm just adding the relation x equals 1.

145
00:45:39,720 --> 00:46:00,600
情况并非总是那么简单：在那个例子中，正如大家在作业中见到的，F[x]/(x^2 - 1) 实际上同构于直积 F ×F。
It doesn't work that way always: in that case, as you saw in the homework, F[x] mod (x^2 - 1) is actually isomorphic to F cross F.

146
00:46:00,600 --> 00:46:10,400
但在本例中，让我们来看看证明，重点梳理几个关键步骤。
But in this simple example, let's just look at the proof, let's just highlight the most important steps.

147
00:46:11,960 --> 00:46:22,800
首先，从多项式环 F[x] 到 F 显然存在一个完全合法的环同态。
So there certainly is a perfectly legitimate ring homomorphism going from F[x] to F.

148
00:46:22,800 --> 00:46:44,760
具体而言，我可以取一个多项式并将它映为其在0 处的求值（代入 0）：这当然是 F 中的元素，并且该映射构成环同态是显然成立的。
Specifically, I can take a polynomial and I can map it to its evaluation at 0: that's certainly an element of F, and it is completely trivial that this thing is actually a ring homomorphism.

149
00:46:44,760 --> 00:47:05,599
而且这个映射是满射，因为只要令 p(x) 为常数多项式 p(x) = c（c ∈ F），那么 φ(p)就是 c，所以该映射确实是满射。
Now this thing is surjective, because if I just let p(x) be the constant polynomial p(x) equals c in F, then phi of p is c, so this thing is indeed surjective.

150
00:47:05,599 --> 00:47:44,760
关键在于，根据第一同构定理，这告诉我们——由第一同构定理可知，在 F[x] 模去该映射 φ 的核与 F 之间存在一个自然同构。
The point is that this tells us, by the first isomorphism theorem— so by the first isomorphism theorem, there is a natural isomorphism between F[x] modulo the kernel of this map phi, and F.

151
00:47:44,760 --> 00:47:54,880
当然，我们的目标是证明其核正好是由 x 生成的理想，即由 x 生成的主理想 (x)。
So of course our goal is to show that the kernel is exactly the ideal generated by x, the principal ideal generated by x.

152
00:47:54,880 --> 00:48:12,389
这并不难看出来：核是所有映到 0 的元素的集合。一个多项式映到 0 当且仅当 0 是p(x) 的根。
Well this is not too hard to see: so the kernel is the set of things which map to 0. Well, a thing maps to 0 if and only if 0 is a root of p(x).

153
00:48:12,389 --> 00:48:24,200
我们在域上已经学过，多项式具有某个根当且仅当 x 减去该根能够整除该多项式。
We saw over fields that a polynomial has a particular root if and only if x minus that root actually divides the polynomial.

154
00:48:24,200 --> 00:48:38,600
所以这成立当且仅当 p(x) = x · q(x)，其中 q 是某个其他多项式，是 F[x] 中的某个多项式。
So this is true if and only if p(x) equals x times q(x), where q is some other polynomial, this is some other polynomial in F[x].

155
00:48:38,600 --> 00:48:46,839
为什么？如何证明我刚才陈述的事实，即有根蕴含这样的整除性？
Why is this? What's a way of showing the fact I just stated, that root implies a divisibility like this?

156
00:48:46,839 --> 00:48:59,839
是的，完全正确：它直接来自于欧几里得带余除法，因为我知道可以写成 p = x · q + r（余式）；但在 0 处对各项求值时，
Yeah, exactly: it follows immediately from the Euclidean algorithm, because I know that I can write p equals x q plus some remainder; but by evaluating all these things at 0,

157
00:48:59,839 --> 00:49:13,720
我得到余式在 0 处的值必须为 0；但是根据带余除法，余式的次数严格小于除式的次数，即小于 1，所以余式必须是常数。
I get that the remainder must be 0 at 0; but the remainder by the Euclidean algorithm has degree less than this, less than the degree of what you're dividing by, so it must be constant.

158
00:49:13,720 --> 00:49:18,760
如果常数在 0 处的值为 0，那么该常数只能是 0。
So if a constant evaluated at 0 is 0, then it must be 0.

159
00:49:18,760 --> 00:49:37,240
而且这可以推广，对任何根都成立。所以我们知道，如果 p(c) = 0，那么作为多项式 p(x) 就等于(x - c) · q(x)。
But this generalizes, this works if I have any root. So, you know, I know that if p(c) equals 0, then p(x) as a polynomial equals (x - c) times q(x).

160
00:49:37,240 --> 00:49:41,599
这是普适的事实。
This is the general fact.

161
00:49:42,760 --> 00:49:52,932
而这个陈述恰恰说明了 p(x) 属于由 x 生成的主理想 (x)。
But this statement is exactly the statement that p(x) is in the principal ideal generated by x.

162
00:49:52,932 --> 00:50:02,160
所以确实，同态的核精确地等于由 x生成的主理想 (x)。
So indeed the kernel is exactly equal to the principal ideal generated by x.

163
00:50:05,000 --> 00:50:08,400
今天就讲到这里。
That's a good place to stop.

164
00:50:09,560 --> 00:50:14,800
祝大家期中考试好运！
Good luck!
